# Everything the images must not see. The build contexts for ops/deploy/Dockerfile.{api,client} are the
# repo root, so a missing entry here means it is copied into a layer and then into the registry — including
# `node_modules` (a 400 MB layer that also breaks `npm ci` reproducibility) and any wallet keypair.
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/target
**/test-ledger
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*-keypair.json
# Rooted on purpose, and the only line in this file that is. `id` is the ISO 639-1 code for Indonesian, so
# five tracked catalogues are named `id.json` (client/src/shared/i18n/{diagnostics,failures,rights}/,
# client/src/shared/lib/legal-copy/, scripts/landing/locales/) and four of them are build inputs:
# client/src/shared/i18n/locales/id.ts imports three, legalCopy.ts imports the fourth. A blanket
# `**/id.json` kept them out of the build context and `vite build` died on "Cannot find module
# './legal-copy/id.json'" — the name-vs-content mistake ci.yml's old `grep -E '(keypair|id)\.json$'` made
# when it burned the security job on the same five files, which scripts/committed-keypairs.ts now settles
# by parsing the body: a 64-uint8 array is a keypair wherever it hides, a locale object never is.
# Rooted, this still excludes what `solana-keygen new -o id.json` and a copied `~/.config/solana/id.json`
# leave at the context root; `**/*-keypair.json` above covers the anchor naming at any depth; and the
# images workflow scans the *built* api image for `id.json`/`*-keypair.json`/`*.env` before anything can
# pull it, so a keypair nested somewhere this list does not name still fails the build there.
id.json
# SEC-B55: `**/.env` is one name out of the five Vite reads — for `vite build` (mode production) it loads
# `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production` and `.env.production.local` from the client root, and every one of
# them can set any `VITE_*` name. process.env wins for the names the Dockerfile declares, so a stray
# undeclared switch (VITE_API_MOCK, VITE_FLAG_DEBUG_PANEL, …) is copied in and baked into a production
# bundle without appearing in any diff of the deploy artifacts. `client/.env.example` literally tells
# developers to "copy to .env.local", so that file is expected to exist on a working machine.
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
ops/deploy/secrets
ops/deploy/backup/*
!ops/deploy/backup/.gitkeep
anchor-clean
coverage
docs
test-results
playwright-report
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/
dapp-store/
guttercaps-landing.html

# Privileged legal evidence and personal team records never belong in source/images.
legal-private/
